Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
How much cavity Wigner negativity can the atomic population record guarantee?\
\
\>", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
A two-level atom exchanges excitations with a single cavity mode. If the \
field begins in a coherent state, its photon-number components drive the atom \
at different Rabi frequencies. The atomic oscillations first lose contrast as \
those components slip out of phase, then recover when some of their phases \
realign. This is collapse and revival.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In a cavity experiment the cheapest thing to record is the atom's \
population: prepare the atom and field, let them interact for a time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 ", detect whether the atom is excited, and repeat. The result is the \
inversion ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["e", "TI"]], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["g", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " as a function of time. The cavity field itself is harder to see. Its \
Wigner function can take negative values, a signature that no classical \
distribution over phase space reproduces, and measuring it requires \
phase-space tomography of the field."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So the question of this essay is: ",
 StyleBox["given only the record ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 StyleBox[", how much Wigner negativity of the cavity field can we guarantee?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " We measure negativity by the negative volume of the Wigner function and \
ask for the largest value that every field compatible with the record must \
reach. Throughout, \"the field\" means the ",
 StyleBox["unconditional cavity state",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": we discard the atom without selecting a measurement outcome."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The answer comes in three steps, each computed below. First, a symmetry of \
the coupling makes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " blind to everything about the field except its photon-number distribution. \
Second, a field with the same photon-number distribution but a random phase \
is a real preparation with the same record, and its negative volume is a \
lower bound for every field with that distribution. Third, the record \
determines the photon-number distribution, so that lower bound is exactly \
what the record guarantees."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["The atom and field: fixing the physical model", "Section",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " span the atomic space ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\:2102", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ". The cavity has Fock states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " photons. Numerically we retain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "-", "1"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 ", so the joint space is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalH]", 
    StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\:2102", "2"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   SuperscriptBox["\:2102", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 ". The atom is always the first subsystem and the field the second."
}], "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The operators ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
     "Ket"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
     "Bra"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-", "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " lower and raise the atom. The field operator obeys ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],
 ". In the rotating-wave approximation, the laboratory Hamiltonian is"
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["c", "TI"]], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"]]}], "2"], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "\[CircleTimes]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["f", "TI"]]}]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{"\[HBar]", 
      StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}], "+", 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["e", "TI"]},
       "Bra"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], 
      RowBox[{
       TemplateBox[{
         StyleBox["g", "TI"]},
        "Bra"], "."}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first two terms are the uncoupled field and atomic energies. The \
interaction converts ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " and back, and the population in that pair oscillates at angular frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 ". We assume resonance, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "+", "1"}]], "\[LessLess]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 ", as required for the rotating-wave model. In the interaction picture the \
free energies disappear, leaving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["I", "TI"]], "=", "\[HBar]", 
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 " with"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["h", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the one-atom specialization of the Hamiltonian in ",
 ButtonBox["Jarvis et al., Eq. (1)",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/html/0812.3766v2"], None}],
 ". We measure time by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

