Cell[TextData[{
 "Have you noticed where the band is widest? In the lossless cavity it is \
broadest between the collapse and the revival, a little after the large-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5613a8b7-1620-2919-7e20-41f1a3d57863"],
 " estimate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "/", "2", "=", "2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ae8fe52-8d2a-0d13-0a97-f01c24df5479"],
 "; at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9a61ac-db6f-0823-69ba-7809de1a5b09"],
 " these asymptotic times run early, and the revival in the record also peaks \
later than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ebbb135-9363-cdcb-4658-297f26179711"],
 ". The middle of that interval is where the large-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fac2774-ed95-ff32-6553-bf318421c218"],
 " picture puts the field's two branches farthest apart. For large ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e0bfcd9-47ee-c5d1-2608-f5837198af3b"],
 " the joint state stays close to a sum of two products, each an atomic state \
times a coherent state whose phase advances by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", 
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SqrtBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bce04d4-edb5-1ec8-29f5-9d9184406412"],
 ", so the field splits into two components that rotate in opposite \
directions around the origin. Near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04eac529-5321-5efa-2ce9-dd7366d424c0"],
 " each has turned by a quarter circle, they sit on opposite sides of the \
origin, and the field is close to a superposition of two coherent states. Its \
interference fringes are the negativity, and they are made of coherences \
between photon numbers: exactly what the record cannot see. Near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "121d8e7a-a943-ef24-4222-2027c8f7b20e"],
 " the two components meet again on the far side of phase space, the atom's \
oscillations return, and the fringe pattern collapses into a smaller \
structure."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"3f53e49d-d2a9-b4ee-6560-fdc6e75d1e34"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Look at the two fields near the large-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "672c7908-ff3c-85a7-0ed4-7155faceef8d"],
 " estimates of those two times. Pick the samples nearest ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f36945c-6fe2-68e0-76cd-0e0609973aca"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250c2a2d-8da6-5f9d-5333-cc77245325e7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"67928f76-a8f6-4c39-0da1-2733c8831703"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"snapshotIndices", " ", "=", " ", 
